{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "The nature and characterization of IT incidents (what the incident is about and its notable operational attributes) as extracted from free-text descriptions",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "incident_category",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Classifies the incident domain (database, email, vpn, etc.), a core facet of characterizing what an incident is about."
    },
    {
      "name": "affected_system_component",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Identifies the specific component affected, refining the category into actionable technical granularity."
    },
    {
      "name": "failure_symptom_type",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Captures the type of failure/symptom, a distinct and coherent facet of incident nature."
    },
    {
      "name": "scope_indicator",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Distinguishes individual vs system-wide vs location-specific impact, a meaningful severity/attention dimension inferable from text."
    },
    {
      "name": "self_resolved_indicator",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "A resolution attribute of the incident; loosely tied to incident characterization though drifting toward lifecycle metadata."
    },
    {
      "name": "cross_assigned_indicator",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "A routing/handling process attribute not derivable from the description content; drifts away from the 'what's in the text' focus."
    },
    {
      "name": "opened_hour_bucket",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Derived from opened_at timestamp, not from the description; a temporal metadata facet unrelated to incident nature inference."
    },
    {
      "name": "recurrence_within_period",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "A cross-record temporal derivation, not a text-inferable characterization of the individual incident's nature."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.6,
  "structure_quality": 0.68,
  "focus_actionability": 0.75,
  "rationale": "The strongest columns (incident_category, affected_system_component, failure_symptom_type, scope_indicator) cohere well around a single inferable focus -- characterizing the nature and impact of incidents from their descriptions -- forming a sound multi-facet structure at useful granularity (domain, component, symptom, scope). However, the set drifts: cross_assigned_indicator, opened_hour_bucket, and recurrence_within_period are process/temporal/cross-record derivations not grounded in the description text, pulling the column set toward a broader 'incident triage metadata' grab-bag rather than one tight focus. This dilutes coherence. The implied focus is genuinely actionable -- an analyst can prioritize by category, scope, and symptom -- but the mixed lifecycle/temporal facets prevent a clean single-focus structure."
}
```

